<style>
  .epfg-post {
    --ink: #172033;
    --muted: #526173;
    --line: #d9e3ea;
    --blue: #2563eb;
    --green: #0f766e;
    --amber: #b45309;
    --red: #b91c1c;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.72;
    max-width: 860px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .epfg-post * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  .epfg-post figure { margin: 0 0 28px; }
  .epfg-post img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .epfg-post h1 {
    margin: 0 0 18px;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 34px;
    line-height: 1.18;
  }
  .epfg-post__hero,
  .epfg-post__inline {
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: #f8fbfd;
  }
  .epfg-post__caption {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 10px 14px;
    background: #f8fbfd;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
  }
  .epfg-post__lead {
    margin: 0 0 24px;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    border-left: 5px solid var(--blue);
    border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
    background: #eef5ff;
  }
  .epfg-post h2 {
    margin: 38px 0 14px;
    padding-top: 8px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    font-size: 25px;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }
  .epfg-post h3 { margin: 22px 0 8px; font-size: 20px; }
  .epfg-post p { margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .epfg-post a {
    color: var(--blue);
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(37, 99, 235, 0.32);
  }
  .epfg-post table {
    width: 100%;
    margin: 14px 0 26px;
    border-collapse: separate;
    border-spacing: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .epfg-post th,
  .epfg-post td {
    padding: 13px 15px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
    text-align: left;
    vertical-align: top;
  }
  .epfg-post th { background: #eaf3ff; color: #17335f; }
  .epfg-post tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
  .epfg-post ol,
  .epfg-post ul { margin: 0 0 24px; padding-left: 22px; }
  .epfg-post li { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .epfg-post__warning {
    margin: 18px 0 24px;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    border: 1px solid #f1c6c6;
    border-left: 5px solid var(--red);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #fff5f5;
    color: #6b1f1f;
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .epfg-post { font-size: 16px; }
    .epfg-post h2 { font-size: 22px; }
    .epfg-post table { display: block; overflow-x: auto; }
    .epfg-post th,
    .epfg-post td { min-width: 170px; }
  }
</style>

<article class="epfg-post">
  <h1>{{ title }}</h1>

  <figure class="epfg-post__hero">
    <img src="{{ image.url or image.path }}" alt="{{ image.alt }}" loading="lazy">
  </figure>

  <p class="epfg-post__lead">{{ lead }}</p>

  <h2>Quick Summary</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for item in quick_summary %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>Applies to / Risk level / Data loss risk / Estimated time / Last checked</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Item</th><th>Details</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Applies to</td><td>{{ facts.applies_to }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Risk level</td><td>{{ facts.risk_level }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Data loss risk</td><td>{{ facts.data_loss_risk }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Estimated time</td><td>{{ facts.estimated_time }}</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Last checked</td><td>{{ facts.last_checked }}</td></tr>
  </table>

  <h2>Before You Start</h2>
  {% for item in before_start %}
  <p>{{ item }}</p>
  {% endfor %}

  <h2>Symptoms</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for item in symptoms %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>What This Usually Means</h2>
  {% for item in meaning %}
  <p>{{ item }}</p>
  {% endfor %}

  {% if inline_images %}
  <figure class="epfg-post__inline">
    <img src="{{ inline_images[0].url or inline_images[0].path }}" alt="{{ inline_images[0].alt }}" loading="lazy">
    <figcaption class="epfg-post__caption">{{ inline_images[0].caption }}</figcaption>
  </figure>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>What Not to Do First</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for item in not_to_do %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>Try This First</h2>
  <ol>
    {% for item in try_first %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

  <h2>Step-by-Step Fixes</h2>
  <ol>
    {% for item in fixes %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

  <h2>After Each Step</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for item in after_each_step %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>What to Record Before Asking for Help</h2>
  <p>Write down the exact message you see, when the problem started, your Windows version, the device model if an accessory is involved, and every fix you already tried. This makes it easier for a support person to separate a Windows setting problem from a hardware, driver, account, network, or app problem.</p>
  <p>If the problem comes and goes, also record the pattern. Note whether it happens after sleep mode, restart, an update, connecting a device, moving to another Wi-Fi network, or opening one specific app. Clear notes prevent repeated risky steps and help you stop before changing advanced settings.</p>

  <h2>Advanced Fixes</h2>
  <div class="epfg-post__warning">Back up important files before advanced fixes. Stop if you see missing files, BitLocker recovery, repeated blue screens, or drive errors.</div>
  <ol>
    {% for item in advanced_fixes %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>

  <h2>When to Stop and Get Help</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for item in stop_help %}
    <li>{{ item }}</li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {% for item in faq %}
  <h3>{{ item.question }}</h3>
  <p>{{ item.answer }}</p>
  {% endfor %}

  <h2>Related Guides</h2>
  <ul>
    {% for item in related_guides %}
    <li><a href="{{ item.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ item.title }}</a></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>Sources</h2>
  <p>Use official Microsoft sources to confirm current Windows behavior before trying advanced fixes.</p>
  <ul>
    {% for source in sources %}
    <li><a href="{{ source.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{{ source.name }}</a></li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <h2>Final Summary</h2>
  <p>{{ title }} should be handled in a safe order. Start with the simple checks, record what changes after each step, and avoid advanced repair steps unless you understand the risk or are following official Microsoft guidance. If the problem affects important files, work, school, or sign-in access, stop and get help before changing deeper system settings.</p>
</article>
